// Local signing override — TEMPLATE.
//
// Copy this file to `Signing.local.xcconfig` (that name is gitignored via
// `*.local.xcconfig`, so it is never committed) and set your certificate hash below.
// It's pulled in by AppShell/Signing.xcconfig's optional `#include?`, so it survives
// `xcodegen generate`.
//
// WHY THIS SHAPE: signing Manually against a specific Apple Development certificate —
// by its SHA-1 hash, with NO DEVELOPMENT_TEAM — produces a real, stable signature with
// Hardened Runtime and needs NO Apple ID account or provisioning profile. That keeps
// TCC grants (Input Monitoring / Accessibility) across rebuilds instead of re-prompting.
//
// Do NOT set DEVELOPMENT_TEAM here: with a team, Xcode demands a provisioning profile
// and fails ("No signing certificate 'Mac Development' found …") unless you've added
// your Apple ID in Xcode → Settings → Accounts. The hash form sidesteps all of that.
//
// Find your cert's hash:
//     security find-identity -p codesigning -v
//       1) 1B2C3D…(40 hex)… "Apple Development: Your Name (TEAMID)"   <- copy this hash
// Pick the "Apple Development" line, not "Developer ID Application". No such cert? Create
// one in Xcode → Settings → Accounts → Manage Certificates → +. Update the hash when the
// cert renews (~yearly). After editing this file just rebuild — no `xcodegen generate`.
CODE_SIGN_STYLE = Manual
CODE_SIGN_IDENTITY = REPLACE_WITH_YOUR_CERT_SHA1_HASH
